# Site name

<!-- Replace the heading with the site's name, and add a line on what the site is and who it's for. -->

A Craft CMS 5 site, built on Club Studio's [`clubstudio/craft`](https://github.com/clubstudio/craft) starter. It runs locally in [DDEV](https://ddev.com/), bundles assets with [Vite](https://vite.dev/) and styles with [Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com).

## Getting started

Install or update [DDEV](https://ddev.com/) (which needs Docker), then, from the project folder, set the project up with a copy of the database:

```
ddev setup path/to/dump.sql.gz
```

This starts DDEV, installs Composer and npm dependencies, creates `.env` with an app ID and security key, imports the database and runs `ddev craft up`. To install Craft from scratch instead, run `ddev setup` without a dump, then `ddev craft install`.

It's safe to run again: it won't overwrite an existing `.env` or keys.

Run `ddev launch` to open the site, and `ddev launch /admin` for the control panel.

## Developing

Start the Vite dev server, with hot reloading, and leave it running while you work:

```
ddev npm run dev
```

Pages render without styles unless it's running. To build optimised, cache-busted assets into `web/dist/`:

```
ddev npm run build
```

Run `ddev stop` when you've finished.

## Commands

Everything runs through DDEV, so nothing else needs installing. These are the commands you'll use most. Run `ddev help` for the full list, or `ddev <command> --help` for a command's options.

### Project

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `ddev setup [dump.sql.gz]` | Set up the project after cloning it, importing the database if one is given |
| `ddev start` / `ddev stop` | Start or stop the project's containers |
| `ddev restart` | Restart, after changing anything in `.ddev/` |
| `ddev launch` | Open the site (`ddev launch /admin` for the control panel) |
| `ddev describe` | Show the project's URLs, services and database details |
| `ddev mailpit` | Open Mailpit, which catches every email the site sends |
| `ddev ssh` | Open a shell in the web container |
| `ddev logs -f` | Follow the web container's logs |
| `ddev poweroff` | Stop every DDEV project |

### Tools

These run inside the web container, so the versions match the ones the site runs on.

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `ddev craft <command>` | Run a Craft console command |
| `ddev composer <command>` | Run Composer |
| `ddev npm <command>` | Run npm |
| `ddev php <file>` | Run PHP |

### Craft

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `ddev craft up` | Run pending migrations and apply project config, after pulling changes |
| `ddev craft project-config/apply` | Apply project config only |
| `ddev craft clear-caches/all` | Clear Craft's caches |
| `ddev craft resave/entries` | Resave entries, after changing fields that affect saved content |

### Database

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `ddev import-db --file=dump.sql.gz` | Replace the local database with a dump |
| `ddev export-db --file=dump.sql.gz` | Export the local database |
| `ddev snapshot` | Save a snapshot of the database, before anything risky |
| `ddev snapshot restore --latest` | Restore the latest snapshot |
| `ddev tableplus` | Open the database in TablePlus, if it's installed |

### Debugging

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `ddev xdebug on` / `ddev xdebug off` | Turn Xdebug on or off. It slows every request, so leave it off when you're not using it |

## Project config

The site's schema (fields, entry types, sections and settings) lives in `config/project/` as YAML, under version control.

- After pulling changes, run `ddev craft up`. It runs any pending migrations, then applies project config to your database.
- In `dev`, schema changes made in the control panel are written back to `config/project/`. Commit the YAML with the templates that use it.

## Templates

```
templates/
├── _layouts/      Document layouts
├── _partials/     Header, footer, skip link
├── _pages/        One template per page entry type
├── _builder/      Reads CMS content and passes it to components
│   └── blocks/    One template per content block
├── _components/   Reusable UI; components take the values they show
│   └── layout/    Container, split and columns, which arrange what's embedded in them
├── _styleguide/   Each component with sample values, at /styleguide in dev mode
└── _macros/       Class maps, transform keys, SVG assets
```

Pages are composed by editors from blocks in the page builder. Image sizes for each layout are set by transform keys in `config/custom.php`.

## MCP

Craft's built-in MCP server lets AI assistants read and manage the site's content and schema in local development only. It answers at `/admin/mcp` when `CRAFT_ENVIRONMENT=dev`, and is switched off everywhere else. In Claude Code, run `/mcp`, choose `craft`, sign in to Craft and approve the request.
